# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
# Per-task worktree venvs (docs/operations/worktree_discipline.md) — never committed.
.venv-wt/
.venv-*/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local render output of scripts/generate_form_archive.py (the publish daemon's archive
# step writes here on every cycle, even in --upload mode; the canonical copy is in Box).
/form_archive_out/

# Local render output of scripts/build_docs_pdfs.py (the §6a enablement PDF manuals; the
# canonical distributable copy is the Box "ITS Manuals" upload — D2-3). Never committed.
/docs/_build_pdf/

# ITS-specific
logs/*.log
logs/**/*.log
# Rotated-log archives written by watchdog Check W (shared/log_rotation.py): daily
# <YYYY-MM-DD>.log.gz + the copy→gz→truncate launchd .out.log.gz siblings. NARROW on
# purpose — `logs/**/*.gz`, NOT `logs/**`, which would swallow the git-TRACKED audit
# output under logs/migrations/ (box_build_*.txt / reclone_*.txt / *.json — none .gz).
logs/**/*.gz
*.local.json
.env
.env.*

# Watchdog last-run markers (scripts/watchdog.py write_last_run_marker)
.watchdog/

# Alert-routing dedupe state file (shared/alert_dedupe.py)
state/

# Credentials must NEVER be committed.
# All secrets live in macOS Keychain — see shared/keychain.py.
*_secret*
*credentials*.json
*.token
*.pem
*.key

# Defensive — some SDKs cache HTTP responses to a local .cache/ dir.
# boxsdk 3.x does not, but the pattern guards against future deps that do.
.cache/

# Defensive — git worktrees for parallel CC sessions live as SIBLINGS of this
# repo (~/its-<task>), never nested inside it (see docs/operations/worktree_discipline.md).
# Sibling worktrees are outside the repo root, so git never sees them — this entry is
# a guard against the one accident that would matter: a worktree mistakenly created at
# the repo root (e.g. `git worktree add its-temp` without `../`), which would otherwise
# show as an untracked dir and could be staged or scanned by repo-relative tooling.
# No legitimate top-level dir is named its-*, so this is zero-false-positive.
/its-*/

# Session scratch — throwaway one-shot scripts a CC session writes while working
# (audit appliers, brief generators, tenant probes). Deliberately NOT part of the
# repo: each is written against a moment's state and is wrong the next day.
#
# Load-bearing, not cosmetic: the dir was untracked but NOT ignored, so `git add -A`
# would stage it — and its contents fail BOTH blocking legs of the CI `test` job
# (ruff E401/I001/F401/E741; mypy import-not-found on modules since renamed). One
# accidental `-A` REDs main. Ignoring it makes that impossible rather than unlikely.
/scratchpad/
